<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adil Shah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adil Shah was a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> who seized power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> after Nader's assassination in 1747. His rule was brief and contested, and he fought a civil war with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-shah">Ibrahim Shah</a> in 1747–1748. These struggles reduced the remnants of the Afsharid state to chaos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adil-shah.jpg" alt="Adil Shah" width="303" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Adel_Shah.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
